## 📖 Introduction

**Agile** is a software development approach that focuses on developing software in **small and frequent increments** instead of building the entire application at once.

Agile encourages:

* 🤝 Team collaboration
* 🔄 Continuous improvement
* 💬 Regular feedback
* 📦 Frequent delivery
* 🎯 Customer satisfaction
* 🔧 Adaptability to changing requirements

> 💡 **Simple Definition:**
> Agile is an iterative and flexible approach where teams develop software in small increments and continuously improve it based on feedback.

---

# 🔄 What is Agile?

Agile follows an **iterative and incremental** development approach.

```text
Plan
  ↓
Design
  ↓
Develop
  ↓
Test
  ↓
Review
  ↓
Feedback
  ↺
```

Instead of waiting until the entire application is complete, Agile teams regularly deliver working increments of the product.

---

# 🎯 Main Goals of Agile

| Goal                          | Description                                         |
| :---------------------------- | :-------------------------------------------------- |
| 🎯 **Customer Satisfaction**  | Deliver useful software according to customer needs |
| ⚡ **Frequent Delivery**       | Deliver working software regularly                  |
| 🔄 **Adaptability**           | Respond effectively to changing requirements        |
| 🤝 **Collaboration**          | Encourage teamwork and communication                |
| 💬 **Continuous Feedback**    | Collect feedback throughout development             |
| 📈 **Continuous Improvement** | Improve the product and process regularly           |

---

# 📜 Agile Manifesto

The **Agile Manifesto** describes four core values:

| Agile Values                        | Preference                       |
| :---------------------------------- | :------------------------------- |
| 👥 **Individuals and interactions** | over processes and tools         |
| 💻 **Working software**             | over comprehensive documentation |
| 🤝 **Customer collaboration**       | over contract negotiation        |
| 🔄 **Responding to change**         | over following a plan            |

> **Important:**
> The items on the right still have value, but Agile places greater emphasis on the items on the left.

