# 🔄 Scrum

**Scrum** is one of the most commonly used Agile frameworks.

Work is organized into fixed-length development cycles called **Sprints**.

```text
Product Backlog
      ↓
Sprint Planning
      ↓
Sprint
      ↓
Working Increment
      ↓
Sprint Review
      ↓
Sprint Retrospective
      ↺
```

---

## 👥 Basic Scrum Roles

| Role                 | Responsibility                                          |
| :------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------ |
| 👤 **Product Owner** | Maximizes product value and manages the Product Backlog |
| 🧭 **Scrum Master**  | Helps the team understand and apply Scrum               |
| 👨‍💻 **Developers** | Build and deliver the product increment                 |

---

# 📋 Product Backlog

The **Product Backlog** is an ordered list of work required for the product.

It may contain:

* New features
* Improvements
* Bug fixes
* Technical work
* Other product requirements

```text
Product Backlog
│
├── User Login
├── User Registration
├── Search Feature
├── Payment Feature
└── Bug Fixes
```

The Product Owner is accountable for effective Product Backlog management and ordering.

