# 📊 Estimation in Agile

Agile estimation helps teams understand the approximate relative effort involved in upcoming work.

Common estimation approaches include:

| Technique                  | Description                                 |
| :------------------------- | :------------------------------------------ |
| 🃏 **Planning Poker**      | Team members estimate using cards or values |
| ⭐ **Story Points**         | Relative estimation of effort               |
| 👕 **T-Shirt Sizing**      | Work classified as XS, S, M, L, XL          |
| 📊 **Relative Estimation** | Compare one work item with another          |

---

# 👕 T-Shirt Sizing

**T-Shirt Sizing** is a simple relative estimation technique.

Tasks or user stories can be classified as:

|  Size  | General Meaning |
| :----: | :-------------- |
| **XS** | Very Small      |
|  **S** | Small           |
|  **M** | Medium          |
|  **L** | Large           |
| **XL** | Very Large      |

Example:

```text
Change Label        → XS
Form Validation     → S
Login Feature       → M
Payment Module      → L
Large Integration   → XL
```

It is useful when teams need a quick high-level estimate.

